[Unit]
# Docker starts its containers itself through their restart policy, so any that
# bind a directory on these volumes race the mount. cryptsetup spends several
# seconds per volume deriving the key with argon2id, and Docker creates a missing
# bind source rather than failing, so losing that race means binding an empty
# directory on the root filesystem: Frigate records there and expires nothing on
# Bay 1, FileBrowser publishes and indexes nothing.
#
# Ordering only, deliberately not Requires: the volumes are mounted with nofail so
# the host boots without the enclosure, and Home Assistant and the other
# containers here have nothing to do with it. A missing enclosure therefore costs
# a boot the device timeout and then starts Docker anyway, at which point the
# containers that need a volume fail loudly, their bind sources being absent.
After={% for volume in nas_volumes | sort(attribute='path') %}{{ volume.path | regex_replace('^/', '') | regex_replace('/', '-') }}.mount{{ ' ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}
